---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What does Jengu do?',
    a: 'We build and run AI agents for hotels and tourism businesses. They handle guest messages across chat, email, SMS, WhatsApp and phone, take and change bookings, do the admin around them, and flag the things that deserve a person’s attention, like a booking that looks likely to cancel.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does setup take?',
    a: 'It depends what we are building. A simple chatbot goes live in two to three weeks, an email agent in three to four, custom software in six to twelve, and a full set of agents in eight to sixteen. Most clients feel the difference in the first month.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do the agents replace our staff?',
    a: 'No. They take the repetitive work so your people have time for the guests in front of them and for the decisions that need judgement.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when the AI gets something wrong?',
    a: 'Every agent has limits we set with you during setup. Anything it is unsure about goes to a person, and it learns from the corrections. We test it hard before it ever talks to a real guest.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which systems do you work with?',
    a: 'Anything with an API. PMS platforms like Opera, Mews and Cloudbeds, booking engines and OTAs like Booking.com, Expedia and Airbnb, CRMs, payment providers and channel managers. Where there is no API, we build the connector.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is guest data safe with you?',
    a: 'Yes. AES-256 encryption, GDPR compliance, secure API connections, role-based access and regular audits. We do not share or sell guest data.',
  },
];
---

<section class="v2-section" data-theme="light" id="faq">
  <div class="v2-container">
    <div class="v2-faq">
      <div class="v2-faq__left">
        <span class="v2-eyebrow" data-reveal>Questions</span>
        <h2 class="v2-h2" data-split>What owners <em>ask us first.</em></h2>
        <p class="v2-lead" data-reveal>Something else on your mind? <a href="/contact" class="v2-serif" style="color: var(--accent)">Ask us.</a></p>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        {
          faqs.map((f, i) => (
            <details open={i === 0}>
              <summary>
                <span>{f.q}</span>
                <i aria-hidden="true" />
              </summary>
              <p class="v2-faq__a">{f.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
